WEBVTT

00:07:28.929 --> 00:07:32.524
So of course, you know,
I am a recent grad,

00:07:32.548 --> 00:07:35.969
I have, at this point,
run all these different experiments,

00:07:35.993 --> 00:07:40.325
I've compiled all this evidence,
and I'd gone into the office of the COO

00:07:40.349 --> 00:07:42.446
and I was raising my concerns.

00:07:43.113 --> 00:07:46.272
"Within the lab, we're seeing
a lot of variability.

00:07:46.296 --> 00:07:48.156
The accuracy rate doesn't seem right.

00:07:48.180 --> 00:07:50.720
I don't feel right
about testing on patients.

00:07:50.744 --> 00:07:53.908
These things, I'm just
not comfortable with."

00:07:53.932 --> 00:07:56.483
And the response I got back is,

00:07:56.507 --> 00:07:58.569
"You don't know
what you're talking about."

00:07:58.593 --> 00:08:01.132
What you need to do
is what I'm paying you to do,